==Welsh==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|cy|myned}} {{qualifier|literary}}

===Etymology===
Suppletive verb; verbal noun from {{etyl|wlm|cy}} {{m|wlm|mynet}}, from {{etyl|cel-bry-pro|cy}} {{m|cel-bry-pro|*monetu}} (compare Cornish {{m|kw|mones}}, Breton {{m|br|mont}}), verbal noun of {{etyl|cel-pro|cy}} {{m|cel-pro|*mon-ī-}} (compare Middle Irish {{m|mga|muinithir||goes around}}), from {{etyl|ine-pro|cy}} {{m|ine-pro|*menH-}} (compare Umbrian {{m|xum|menes||will come}}, Lithunaian {{m|lt|mìnti||to trample, scutch}}). Indicative forms from {{etyl|cel-pro|cy}} {{m|cel-pro|*ago-||to drive}} (compare Old Irish {{m|sga|aigid}}), from {{etyl|ine-pro|cy}} {{m|ine-pro|*h₂eǵ-}} (compare Latin {{m|la|agō}}). The forms in ''el-'' are from {{etyl|cel-pro|cy}} {{m|cel-pro|*ɸel-||to approach, drive}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|cy}} {{m|ine-pro|*pelh₂-}} (compare Latin {{m|la|pellō||strike, drive}}, Epic Greek {{m|grc|πίλναμαι||approach}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|North Wales}} {{IPA|[mɨ̞nd]|lang=cy}}
* {{a|South Wales}} {{IPA|[mɪnd]|lang=cy}}

===Verb===
{{head|cy|verb|irregular}}

# to [[go]]
#: {{usex|Mae hi'n '''mynd''' i Gaerdydd heno.|inline=1|t=She's going to Cardiff tonight.|lang=cy}}
#: {{usex|'''Aeth''' hi ddoe.|inline=1|t=She went yesterday.|lang=cy}}
#: {{usex|'''Awn''' ni ac yn edrych.|inline=1|t=We will go and look.|lang=cy}}
#: {{usex|'''Aet''' ti i'r ysgol ar droed.|inline=1|t=You went/used to go to school on foot.|lang=cy}}
#: {{usex|Mae'n angenrheidiol yr '''elwyf''' nawr.|inline=1|t=It is necessary that I go now.|lang=cy}}
#: {{usex|Na, rwy'n '''mynd''' ar y trên bach.|t=No, I'm taking the little train.|inline=1|lang=cy}}

